      "writtenOn": "2016-10-20T20:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Similar to Etan\u0027s comment on line 34... Prefer not to use spaces, as it complicates log processing.\n\nWithout spaces, we can do some pretty decent log processing using simple command-line tools like sed/awk/split/join. Spaces makes this much harder.\n\nConcretely, consider something like\n\n  mTag \u003d serviceTag + \".\" + \"asyncChannel\";\n\nThe dot syntax, and the change in ordering, conveys the idea that the async channel is part of the service, by borrowing from the syntax we use in source code itself.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "7631779874f6daf60cf94528b753e49b612117a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
